WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.468
Same gauge. Nothing has been calibrated, adjusted, or replaced.

2
00:00:05.566 --> 00:00:09.140
Act A left two names under one band. Both

3
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.186
go. The band goes on a plant rail.

4
00:00:12.283 --> 00:00:17.511
A ruler against it. Not a caption about the width, the width itself.

5
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:24.628
Six sigma of gauge, end to end: 12.4 microns. It does not move again.

6
00:00:24.716 --> 00:00:28.024
Two plants are about to divide by different

7
00:00:28.124 --> 00:00:31.432
things. This is the thing they both divide.

8
00:00:31.516 --> 00:00:34.329
This plant has to put parts in the right

9
00:00:34.429 --> 00:00:37.896
bin, and the parts are close together on purpose.

10
00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:41.659
One feature, two process families, sitting

11
00:00:41.759 --> 00:00:44.267
exactly one gauge band apart.

12
00:00:44.366 --> 00:00:48.016
Here is the truth. Every part where it really is,

13
00:00:48.116 --> 00:00:51.154
each on its own side of the sorting line.

14
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.390
Now read the same parts through the band.

15
00:00:54.483 --> 00:00:58.740
The truth left a 2.05 micron gap. The readings

16
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.329
overlap by 7.53, filled and open marks interleaved. Nothing

17
00:01:04.429 --> 00:01:08.687
came between the two pictures except the band.

18
00:01:08.783 --> 00:01:12.649
A second masked plant. The first greys out at the

19
00:01:12.749 --> 00:01:16.939
edge of frame: two jobs, one instrument between them.

20
00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:20.583
This plant does not care which parts differ. It

21
00:01:20.683 --> 00:01:23.845
has to say pass or fail against a drawing.

22
00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:28.302
The process is wide: 151 microns against a

23
00:01:28.402 --> 00:01:32.665
drawing of 35, and nobody is fixing that.

24
00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:37.066
Lay the same band on the upper limit. Same object, same

25
00:01:37.166 --> 00:01:41.242
width. Every part under it can be called either way.

26
00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:45.094
2 good parts read as scrap. 3 bad parts read as

27
00:01:45.194 --> 00:01:49.201
good. From the band that could not sort next door.

28
00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:54.264
Same width, a different kind of mistake, and still no percentage.

29
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:59.506
Both plants in one frame, so the choice is made side by side.

30
00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.313
One band each. The second is a copy sliding out

31
00:02:03.413 --> 00:02:08.020
of the first, so the widths are identical by construction.

32
00:02:08.116 --> 00:02:12.744
Before a percentage exists, say what you are dividing by.

33
00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.493
Two candidates per plant: how much its parts

34
00:02:16.593 --> 00:02:19.853
differ, and how much room its drawing gives.

35
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.152
Drop the drawing under the sorting plant. A

36
00:02:23.252 --> 00:02:27.146
legal move, answering a question nobody there asked.

37
00:02:27.233 --> 00:02:30.747
The numerators are identical, so this is not a

38
00:02:30.847 --> 00:02:34.832
fact about the gauge. The job picks: sorting divides

39
00:02:34.932 --> 00:02:38.053
by the study, conformance by the drawing.

40
00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:41.040
Both fractions are complete, and there is

41
00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.594
still no percentage on this screen.

42
00:02:43.683 --> 00:02:46.879
Two plants, two jobs. Four questions, and

43
00:02:46.979 --> 00:02:50.015
the other two are the interesting ones.

44
00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.668
One band, feeding four cells. Rows are the plants, columns

45
00:02:54.768 --> 00:02:59.096
the jobs. Which cells earn use, and which earn replace?

46
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:04.127
The cells each plant asked for, on the diagonal. Both asked

47
00:03:04.227 --> 00:03:08.771
the question their gauge is worst at, so both read replace.

48
00:03:08.866 --> 00:03:11.284
Now the cells nobody asked for.

49
00:03:11.384 --> 00:03:14.694
Same band, same gates, different question.

50
00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:18.841
Hold the job still, move the gauge between plants.

51
00:03:18.941 --> 00:03:24.163
Sort process populations: replace, then use. Nothing else moved.

52
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:28.188
Hold the job still, move the gauge between plants.

53
00:03:28.288 --> 00:03:33.438
Judge drawing conformance: use, then replace. Nothing else moved.

54
00:03:33.533 --> 00:03:38.449
Both of these are honest. They are answers to different questions.

55
00:03:38.533 --> 00:03:42.635
The middle band is still empty and still uncoloured.

56
00:03:42.735 --> 00:03:46.353
Improve is a next action, not a third verdict.

57
00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:50.046
A second number is printed in the same table.

58
00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:53.672
Number of distinct categories: how many groups

59
00:03:53.772 --> 00:03:56.441
of parts this gauge can tell apart.

60
00:03:56.533 --> 00:04:00.616
One curve. Every ndc a gauge can have against the

61
00:04:00.716 --> 00:04:04.713
study ratio it came from, falling the whole way.

62
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:10.556
Both plants, computed the long way from the gauge and the parts,

63
00:04:10.656 --> 00:04:15.589
land on it. Not near it: the two routes differ by under

64
00:04:15.689 --> 00:04:20.348
4e-15. The only thing ndc adds is the constant 1.41.

65
00:04:20.433 --> 00:04:25.931
Now the printed gates: ten per cent, thirty per cent, five categories. All

66
00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:30.773
three come off the same table, and the last two miss each other.

67
00:04:30.866 --> 00:04:37.041
2.86 points apart. The ndc rule bites first, at 27.1 per cent,

68
00:04:37.141 --> 00:04:43.822
inside the middle band where the action reads improve in plain ink.

69
00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:47.513
One of these two printed rules is stricter than the

70
00:04:47.613 --> 00:04:50.992
other, and the table they share does not say so.

71
00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:54.884
Everything this act built, in order, for one plant.

72
00:04:54.984 --> 00:04:58.327
Which link is the only choice a person makes?

73
00:04:58.816 --> 00:05:03.193
They fly in from where they were earned: the job from the plants,

74
00:05:03.293 --> 00:05:08.220
the denominator from the fractions, the rest from the grid and the gates.

75
00:05:08.316 --> 00:05:12.108
Only the first link was a decision. The rest is

76
00:05:12.208 --> 00:05:16.496
arithmetic and a lookup, and the band never joins in.

77
00:05:16.583 --> 00:05:21.163
Swap the job token, and touch nothing else on the screen.

78
00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:25.098
Same plant, same parts, same band. One word at the

79
00:05:25.198 --> 00:05:29.046
front, and the last four links moved. Put it back.

80
00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:32.195
The gauge does not own a verdict. The job

81
00:05:32.295 --> 00:05:36.977
chooses the denominator, and the denominator carries the rest.

